---
/**
 * /ai-fit/ — the AI Fit Assessment. THE SECOND PAID THING ON THIS SITE.
 *
 * ONE FORM SINCE 2026-09-20 (D118). The in-business form, the rule that
 * assigned a form, the drive that bounded it and the second figure all left
 * with the three-door decision; what is sold is ninety minutes on video, at
 * one flat figure, with the whole fee credited against a build. It is reached
 * from the local door rather than a header seat. Every paragraph below about
 * two forms and the buyer never picking is the record of 2026-09-06 to
 * 2026-09-20 and is kept as that.
 *
 * WHY IT ENDS IN A PRICED BUILD LIST RATHER THAN A REPORT. src/data/home.ts's
 * `comparison`, rendered on /approach/, heads a column "What AI consulting
 * usually ends with" and lists `An "AI readiness" audit` inside it. Selling an
 * assessment whose deliverable is a document would put this practice's own
 * named failure mode on its own price list, two clicks from the page saying so.
 *
 * The distinction is not wording, it is the last page. A roadmap says what to
 * think about. This says what to build, what each one costs, and which one goes
 * first — which is a quote with its reasoning attached, and quoting is already
 * what this practice does. That is why /approach/ needs no edit and never has to
 * argue with itself: the difference lives here, in "What this is not".
 *
 * TWO FORMS SINCE 2026-09-06, AND THE VISITOR PICKS NEITHER. This page carried
 * one price and one form until then, and the sentence it carried was "Wherever I
 * can drive to you, that is included — there is no separate visit fee and no
 * cheaper version without it." Both halves were false by the end: the signed
 * agreement committed to half a day or a day while this page said an hour, and
 * $1,000 covers the first of those and not the second.
 *
 * THE WHOLE SHAPE RESTS ON ONE THING: THE BUYER DOES NOT CHOOSE. D81 records
 * this and the three measured things behind it. D61 refused a
 * two-tier pair because a buyer cannot judge what a visit is worth before having
 * one, so nearly all take the cheaper and the better form never sells. That is
 * correct, and it assumes the buyer is choosing. Here the rule is PRINTED ABOVE
 * THE FIGURES so a reader applies it to themselves before making contact, and it
 * lives once in src/data/services.ts because the signed agreement states the
 * same rule in prose. D5 survives for the same reason: a menu asks you to pick a
 * version of yourself, and nobody picks here.
 *
 * SO NOTHING ON THIS PAGE MAY LET A VISITOR SELECT A FORM. No radio, no pair of
 * pay buttons, no two links differing only by price. scripts/verify-assessment.mjs
 * asserts the absence, because that is the one part of this no comment can hold.
 * It is also why the pay button LEFT this page on 2026-09-06: two buttons is the
 * visitor choosing, and one button cannot know which form they need. The links
 * still live in src/lib/payments.js and the right one is sent after the form is
 * assigned.
 *
 * WHY THE FEE IS CREDITED, AND WHY ONLY PART OF IT ON THE VISIT. Uncredited, an
 * assessment ending in a priced build makes that build cost more than buying it
 * directly — the document would argue against its own recommendation, and a
 * buyer does that arithmetic out loud. A fixed credit erases it on the video form
 * entirely. On the visit it leaves the buyer paying for the one thing that was
 * never a discount waiting to happen. Full argument above ASSESSMENT_VIDEO_USD
 * in src/lib/pricing.js.
 *
 * EVERY FIGURE AND ITS QUALIFIER ARE ONE OBJECT. Rendering `.amount` without
 * `.qualifier` publishes a fee and hides the credit, which is a different and
 * worse offer. Same rule, same reason, as startingPrice.
 *
 * THE META DESCRIPTION CARRIES NO FIGURE, changed 2026-09-06. There are two now,
 * a figure without its qualifier is a worse offer than the one being sold, and
 * neither pair fits inside the ~160 characters a search result shows.
 *
 * ITS OWN SHARE CARD SINCE 2026-09-03. It shared /og/default.png before, so a
 * link posted to LinkedIn or Nextdoor showed a picture saying nothing about the
 * assessment — on the page where a share is most likely to be somebody's first
 * contact with this practice. The card carries NO figure, for the reason above:
 * the price and its credit are one statement and neither fits on a card.
 */
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { assessmentPrice, startingPrice } from '../data/services';
import { ASSESSMENT_VIDEO_USD } from '../lib/pricing.js';
import { Search, Footprints, ListChecks, ArrowUpRight } from '@lucide/astro';

const origin = new URL(Astro.site!).origin;

const steps = [
  {
    icon: Footprints,
    n: '01',
    t: 'I watch the work happen',
    b: 'Your screen shared while you do the job, so I see the real file rather than a description of it, and where the job happens away from a screen you show me on camera. I look instead of asking, because the things costing you money are the ones nobody thinks to mention.',
  },
  {
    icon: Search,
    n: '02',
    t: 'I go through how it actually runs today',
    b: 'The spreadsheet somebody rebuilt, the thing that gets re-typed into two systems, the job that only one person knows how to do. I want the workarounds, not the org chart — a workaround is a business telling you exactly where its software stopped.',
  },
  {
    icon: ListChecks,
    n: '03',
    t: 'You get it in writing, with numbers beside it',
    b: 'A short document naming what is worth doing, what is not, what each one would cost to build, and which I would do first and why. It is yours whether or not you ever hire me, and it is written so another developer could work from it.',
  },
];

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'Service',
    '@id': `${origin}/ai-fit/#service`,
    name: 'AI Fit Assessment',
    serviceType: 'Operational assessment and build scoping',
    provider: { '@id': `${origin}/#organization` },
    areaServed: 'US',
    description:
      'A read of how the work is actually done, on video, and a written list of what is worth building, each with a price beside it. The whole fee comes off a build.',
    offers: {
      '@type': 'Offer',
      name: 'AI Fit Assessment — on video',
      price: ASSESSMENT_VIDEO_USD,
      priceCurrency: 'USD',
      description: assessmentPrice.video.qualifier,
    },
  },
  {
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${origin}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Main Street', item: `${origin}/main-street/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'AI Fit Assessment', item: `${origin}/ai-fit/` },
    ],
  },
];
---
<MarketingLayout
  schema={schema}
  title="AI Fit Assessment"
  description="Where AI actually fits your business, and where it does not. Ninety minutes on video, then a written list of what is worth building with a price beside each line."
  image="/og/ai-fit.png"
>
  {/* ── Hero ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      D113 CARRIED OFF THE HOME PAGE, 2026-09-13. This page ran three bands at
      6xl, 5xl, 3xl on one ground and one rhythm — and the last of them held
      THREE blocks built identically, a `border-t border-line pt-10` wrapper
      over a mono-label over a heading over prose. That is D113's complaint one
      level down from where D113 found it, running three times in a row on the
      page that does the most turning-away.

      Five bands now. The column walks feature, content, popout, content,
      popout; the ground walks canvas, surface, canvas, deep, surface; the
      rhythm moves under all of it. No two neighbors share more than one heavy
      signal and the palette does none of the work.

      NOTHING INSIDE THIS BAND MOVED, and that is not caution. The order here is
      load-bearing and measured: verify-assessment.mjs asserts the assignment
      rule arrives BEFORE both figures, that each figure's credit sits within
      400 rendered characters of it, and that the second destination sits within
      600 of the video line. The shape may change around this band; the sequence
      inside it may not. */}
  <Section width="feature" class="border-b border-line">
    <Fragment slot="backdrop">
      <div class="bg-grid bg-grid-fade pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 opacity-60"></div>
    </Fragment>
      <p class="mono-label">A read of the work · a written answer · a price beside every line</p>
      <h1 class="statement mt-3 max-w-3xl">
        Everyone says you should be using AI. Nobody says <span class="aiq-accent">where</span>.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        That is the actual problem, and it is not a knowledge gap you can read your way out of. What
        fits depends on how your business really runs, which is why I go and look at it rather than
        sending you a questionnaire.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        You end up holding a list of what is worth building, in order, with a number beside each one.
      </p>

      {/* ONE FIGURE AND ITS QUALIFIER IN ONE PANEL, since 2026-09-20 (D118). The
          rule that used to arrive before two figures left with the second form;
          verify-assessment.mjs still asserts the credit is painted within 400
          rendered characters of the figure. */}
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-2xl">
        <div class="panel flex flex-col gap-2 p-6">
          <p class="font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">{assessmentPrice.video.line}</p>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{assessmentPrice.video.qualifier}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">{assessmentPrice.video.whatItIs}</p>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">{assessmentPrice.video.whoItIsFor}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        {assessmentPrice.credit.line} If you never build anything, you still keep the document — and it is
        written for any developer, not only for me.
      </p>

      {/* THERE IS NO PAY BUTTON HERE, AND THAT IS FORCED RATHER THAN CHOSEN.
          Two buttons is the visitor picking a form, which is the one thing this
          page cannot let them do — see the block at the top of this file. One
          button cannot know which form they need, and a button charging the
          wrong amount is worse than no button. The links live in
          src/lib/payments.js and the right one is sent once the form is
          assigned, which is a sentence in an email rather than machinery.
          scripts/verify-payments.mjs asserts the absence. */}
      <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a href="/contact/?intent=assessment" class="btn btn-primary">Ask about an assessment →</a>
        <a href="/check/" class="btn btn-secondary">Or run the free check first</a>
      </div>
  </Section>

  {/* ── What happens ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <Section tone="surface" width="content">
    <p class="mono-label">What happens</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-2xl font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">
      Three things, and the first one is me looking rather than asking.
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
      {steps.map((s) => (
        <div class="panel lift flex flex-col gap-3 p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <s.icon class="h-5 w-5 text-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span class="mono-label">{s.n}</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-ink">{s.t}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{s.b}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </Section>

  {/* ── What this is not — the section that keeps /approach/ honest ──────────
       THE THREE BLOCKS THAT LIVED IN ONE SECTION ARE THREE BANDS NOW, and each
       lost the `border-t border-line pt-10` wrapper it used to open with: every
       band edge already paints that rule, and a second hairline forty pixels
       under it read as a mistake rather than as structure. Nothing moved — the
       order is the order it was written in, which is refusal, then assumption,
       then the only claim on the page about the person doing the work. */}
  <Section width="popout" density="tall">
      <p class="mono-label">What this is not</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">
        Not a strategy deck, and not a readiness score.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        There is no maturity rating, no roadmap, no vendor shortlist, and no comparison against
        companies I have never seen. Every line in the document is a thing that could be built, with
        what it would cost to build it, because a recommendation you cannot price is just an opinion
        with a font.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        I am not selling you AI either. If the honest answer is that a whiteboard and a changed
        Tuesday routine would fix it, that is what the document says, and you still keep the
        document. Plenty of the best work I have done for a business had no AI anywhere near it.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        And it is not a first conversation. That is still free, still has no assessment attached, and
        is still the right place to start if you already know what you want built.
        {' '}{startingPrice.line} {startingPrice.qualifier}
      </p>
  </Section>

  {/* ── What it assumes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       Written in the voice of "What this is not" directly above, and for the
       same reason: turning somebody away in print makes every other claim on
       the page more believable. Each of these was a silence before 2026-09-06,
       and a silence is what a buyer fills in optimistically.

       THE DEEP GROUND IS SPENT HERE. It is the heaviest signal the page has and
       this is the band that costs the seller something, which is the one worth
       making a reader stop at. It is also safe on it: nothing in here is a
       panel or a border literal sized for a light ground, which is the trap
       that sent /work/ and /websites/ to `deep` rather than `instrument`, and
       the definition list is dt/dd — both named in the rule that strips the
       canvas-colored text-shadow off a deep band. The wider column is for the
       list itself, which ran two columns inside a reading measure. */}
  <Section tone="deep" width="content">
      <p class="mono-label">What it assumes</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">
        Four things, so nothing is a surprise later.
      </h2>
      <dl class="mt-6 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <dt class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">One business, one place.</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            The price covers one location. If you run four, the other three are quoted separately,
            because four locations is four reads and not one.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">It happens while the work does.</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            There is nothing to watch in an empty building or a closed screen, so we go when the job
            is actually being done. That is usually your busiest hour, and that is the point.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">It happens in an evening, on video.</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            The plant's planning floor has my weekdays, so the session is an evening set ahead, and
            most evenings work. Where the job happens away from a screen, you show me on camera.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">A business with no repeated job has nothing to assess.</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            What this finds is work that repeats and costs you time. Where there is none, there is
            nothing to price, and I would rather say that before taking the money than after.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="surface" width="popout" density="tight">
      <p class="mono-label">Why me</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">
        I have stood on the floor in most of these businesses.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        A restaurant floor at a casino for five and a half years. A bank's lending division, then
        cash management at a second bank. A clinical practice's scheduling and records. A licensed
        insurance practice. Now the planning floor of the appliance plant in town. That is not a
        credential I am waving — it is why I can watch your work and know which part of it is unusual,
        which is the only skill this job actually needs.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        <a href="/contact/?intent=assessment" class="btn btn-primary">
          Ask about an assessment <ArrowUpRight class="h-4 w-4" aria-hidden="true" />
        </a>
        <a href="/bio/" class="btn btn-secondary">The whole run of it</a>
      </div>
  </Section>
</MarketingLayout>
